{
  "title": "ISic001368. Funerary inscription for Sabina",
  "body": "<div id=\"editions\"><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Alex Antoniou</div><div id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  <div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  <a id=\"al1-interpretive\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"σὺν\">σὺν</span>  <span data-text=\"θεῷ\">θεῷ</span> (Χριστῷ) <span data-text=\"καὶ\">κ(αὶ)</span>  <span data-text=\"πατρι\">[πατρι]</span>  <br id=\"al2-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-text=\"αὐτοῦ\">αὐτοῦ</span>  <span data-text=\"ἐκοιμήθη\">ἐκοιμ[ήθη]</span>  <br id=\"al3-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span><span data-text=\"ἡ\">ἡ</span>  <span data-text=\"δούλη\">δούλη</span>  <span data-text=\"τοῦ\">τοῦ</span>  <span data-text=\"θεοῦ\">[θεοῦ]</span>  <br id=\"al4-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Σαβεῖνα\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Σαβεῖνα\">Σαβεῖνα</span></span>  <span data-text=\"τῇ\">τῇ</span>  <span data-text=\"πρὸ\">[πρὸ]</span>  <br id=\"al5-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span>τρειῶν´ <span data-text=\"Εἰδῶν\">Εἰδῶν</span>  </span></div>  <p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Alex Antoniou</div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\"><div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><a id=\"al1-diplomatic\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"σὺν\">ΣΥΝ</span><span data-text=\"θεῷ\">ΘΕΩ</span>𐆠<span data-text=\"καὶ\">Κ</span><span data-text=\"πατρι\">[.....]</span><br id=\"al2-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-text=\"αὐτοῦ\">ΑΥΤΟΥ</span><span data-text=\"ἐκοιμήθη\">ΕΚΟΙΜ[...]</span><br id=\"al3-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span><span data-text=\"ἡ\">Η</span><span data-text=\"δούλη\">ΔΟΥΛΗ</span><span data-text=\"τοῦ\">ΤΟΥ</span><span data-text=\"θεοῦ\">[....]</span><br id=\"al4-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Σαβεῖνα\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Σαβεῖνα\">ΣΑΒΕΙΝΑ</span></span><span data-text=\"τῇ\">ΤΗ</span><span data-text=\"πρὸ\">[...]</span><br id=\"al5-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span>ΤΡΕΙΩΝ<span data-text=\"Εἰδῶν\">ΕΙΔΩΝ</span></span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span><span>Text: IG with emendation from Ferrua</span></span>; </li><li><span class=\"line 1\">line.1: <span>IG and CIG record Latin cross, Staurogram supplied by Ferrua</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"lines 1-2\">lines.1-2: <span>σὺν θεῷ Χρ(ιστῷ) κ(αὶ) [πατρὶ] | αὐτοῦ Agnello; σὺν θεῷ κ(αὶ) [τῷ Χ(ριστ)ῷ] vel σὺν θεῷ κ(αὶ) [τῷ ὑῷ] | αὐτοῦ CIG IV 9479; σὺν θεῷ κ(αὶ) [τῷ ὑῷ] | αὐτοῦ IG XIV 549</span></span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo</a></p>  <p>With God, Christ and His Father, the servant of God Sabina fell asleep three days before the Ides of ...</p>  </div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>The Christian funerary inscription opens with the formula <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">σὺν θεῷ Χρ(ιστῷ) κ(αὶ) [πατρὶ] | αὐτοῦ</span> (ll. 1–2). The deceased, named Sabina (cf. NScav. 1905, 397 no. 3, from Syracuse; IG XIV 264 (<a href=\"https://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic001083\" target=\"_blank\">ISic001083</a>), from Agrigento), is described by the formula <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">ἡ δούλη τοῦ [θεοῦ]</span> (l. 3), which is characteristic of Christian funerary inscriptions (cf. Grossi Gondi 1920, 139–162).</p>  </div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Kirchhoff 1877 9479 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001249\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001249</a></li><li> Kaibel 1890 <a href=\"https://clio.columbia.edu/catalog/6873760\" target=\"_blank\">549</a>  <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072</a></li><li> Ferrua 1938 68 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002004\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002004</a></li><li> Agnello 1953 no.55 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002211\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002211</a></li></ul>  <ul><li> Grossi Gondi 1920 139–162 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002241\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002241</a>  </li></ul>  </div>  <div id=\"handnote\"> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    </div><div id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.  </div>",
  "divs": [
    {
      "id": "editions",
      "html": "<div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Alex Antoniou</div><div id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  <div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  <a id=\"al1-interpretive\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"σὺν\">σὺν</span>  <span data-text=\"θεῷ\">θεῷ</span> (Χριστῷ) <span data-text=\"καὶ\">κ(αὶ)</span>  <span data-text=\"πατρι\">[πατρι]</span>  <br id=\"al2-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-text=\"αὐτοῦ\">αὐτοῦ</span>  <span data-text=\"ἐκοιμήθη\">ἐκοιμ[ήθη]</span>  <br id=\"al3-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span><span data-text=\"ἡ\">ἡ</span>  <span data-text=\"δούλη\">δούλη</span>  <span data-text=\"τοῦ\">τοῦ</span>  <span data-text=\"θεοῦ\">[θεοῦ]</span>  <br id=\"al4-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Σαβεῖνα\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Σαβεῖνα\">Σαβεῖνα</span></span>  <span data-text=\"τῇ\">τῇ</span>  <span data-text=\"πρὸ\">[πρὸ]</span>  <br id=\"al5-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span>τρειῶν´ <span data-text=\"Εἰδῶν\">Εἰδῶν</span>  </span></div>  <p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Alex Antoniou</div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\"><div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><a id=\"al1-diplomatic\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"σὺν\">ΣΥΝ</span><span data-text=\"θεῷ\">ΘΕΩ</span>𐆠<span data-text=\"καὶ\">Κ</span><span data-text=\"πατρι\">[.....]</span><br id=\"al2-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span><span data-text=\"αὐτοῦ\">ΑΥΤΟΥ</span><span data-text=\"ἐκοιμήθη\">ΕΚΟΙΜ[...]</span><br id=\"al3-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span><span data-text=\"ἡ\">Η</span><span data-text=\"δούλη\">ΔΟΥΛΗ</span><span data-text=\"τοῦ\">ΤΟΥ</span><span data-text=\"θεοῦ\">[....]</span><br id=\"al4-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span><span data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Σαβεῖνα\"><span data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Σαβεῖνα\">ΣΑΒΕΙΝΑ</span></span><span data-text=\"τῇ\">ΤΗ</span><span data-text=\"πρὸ\">[...]</span><br id=\"al5-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span>ΤΡΕΙΩΝ<span data-text=\"Εἰδῶν\">ΕΙΔΩΝ</span></span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "apparatus",
      "html": "<h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span><span>Text: IG with emendation from Ferrua</span></span>; </li><li><span class=\"line 1\">line.1: <span>IG and CIG record Latin cross, Staurogram supplied by Ferrua</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"lines 1-2\">lines.1-2: <span>σὺν θεῷ Χρ(ιστῷ) κ(αὶ) [πατρὶ] | αὐτοῦ Agnello; σὺν θεῷ κ(αὶ) [τῷ Χ(ριστ)ῷ] vel σὺν θεῷ κ(αὶ) [τῷ ὑῷ] | αὐτοῦ CIG IV 9479; σὺν θεῷ κ(αὶ) [τῷ ὑῷ] | αὐτοῦ IG XIV 549</span></span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "translation",
      "html": "<h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo</a></p>  <p>With God, Christ and His Father, the servant of God Sabina fell asleep three days before the Ides of ...</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "commentary",
      "html": "<h2>commentary</h2>  <p>The Christian funerary inscription opens with the formula <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">σὺν θεῷ Χρ(ιστῷ) κ(αὶ) [πατρὶ] | αὐτοῦ</span> (ll. 1–2). The deceased, named Sabina (cf. NScav. 1905, 397 no. 3, from Syracuse; IG XIV 264 (<a href=\"https://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic001083\" target=\"_blank\">ISic001083</a>), from Agrigento), is described by the formula <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">ἡ δούλη τοῦ [θεοῦ]</span> (l. 3), which is characteristic of Christian funerary inscriptions (cf. Grossi Gondi 1920, 139–162).</p>  "
    },
